rs (good crew), but communication difficulty and egocentric. D has responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but moody and loner.\n\nWe need to weigh. Perhaps B's concerns are less severe than C's? Pretentious and wrong tone could affect crew cooperation significantly. C's unfriendly and show-off also affect crew. Both have issues. Which strengths outweigh? C's anticipation of dangerous situations is crucial for safety. B's stress handling is also important. But C's leadership is strong. I think C still strongest overall, but we need to bring up other candidates for coverage. So we can say we still favor C but note we need to discuss A, B, D. Provide some evidence for B to compare.\n\nThus our public message: I agree with C but raise concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability, and suggest we examine B's conscientiousness and stress handling as alternative. Provide facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, but pretentious and wrong tone. Then state provisional vote remains C.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nMetadata: vote Candidate C."}
